os","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> From a pure readability perspective I do find some of the cases a readability concern when nestled inside the macro though\r\n\r\nI agree with this. I'm too used to these macros having conditionals that do not make any behavioral difference and only exist for validation, while the code inside this macro can and will make differences. I'd say it makes the code feel inconsequential?","created_at":"2026-07-23T15:59:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T16:00:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#discussion_r3639554825","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121617","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3639554825"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121617#discussion_r3639554825"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121617"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3639554825/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":554,"original_start_line":554,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":557,"original_line":557,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3637542670,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":97,"position":97,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3639573268","pull_request_review_id":4765933393,"id":3639573268,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y73sU","diff_hunk":"@@ -576,12 +552,9 @@ Error JSON::_parse_string(const String &p_json, Variant &r_ret, String &r_err_st\n \tToken token;\n \tr_err_line = 0;\n \n-\tError err = _get_token(str, idx, len, token, r_err_line, r_err_str);\n-\tif (err) {\n-\t\treturn err;\n-\t}\n+\tGUARD_OK(_get_token(str, idx, len, token, r_err_line, r_err_str));\n \n-\terr = _parse_value(r_ret, token, str, idx, len, r_err_line, 0, r_err_str);\n+\tError err = _parse_value(r_ret, token, str, idx, len, r_err_line, 0, r_err_str);","path":"core/io/json.cpp","commit_id":"00120405f4e26933b6a4429331a7d0d0b3a60dc3","original_commit_id":"d8d701977c82dd8f8c96a293de1503a4256435c0","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"That's another angle I didn't consider, I just meant the readability of the block of text inside the macro, but the expectation here is important to convey\r\n\r\nI'm also generally hesitant to put *mutating* code inside error macros from a stability perspective and to make it easier to navigate checking code and strip it out, but that's a bit tangential (essentially I tend to prefer to keep code that does things rather than checks things outside of any error checking macros, so that you can conceptually strip all error checking macros and retain behavior assuming correct usage)","create